{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"People run language models on their own computers because the cloud is convenient, but it is not always the right fit. For many users, the main reason is privacy. Prompts, documents, code, medical notes, legal drafts, or personal conversations can reveal sensitive information. Keeping the model local means that data does not have to leave the device, and the user has more control over what is stored, shared, or logged. For individuals and small teams, this can matter more than the ease of a hosted API.\n\nCost is another factor. Cloud services often charge per token, per request, or by subscription tier, which can become expensive for heavy use. A local model requires upfront hardware and maintenance, but once it is running, use can be more predictable and less dependent on usage limits. For people who experiment often, build tools, or run many small tasks, that can be attractive.\n\nLocal models","reasoning_content":"The user wants a short essay in English about why people run language models on their own computers instead of in the cloud. Need produce final answer only. Need ensure essay is short, coherent, maybe 4-6 paragraphs or ~300-450 words. Need discuss privacy, cost, control, latency/offline, customization, data sovereignty, security, independence from providers, hardware/performance, experimentation. Avoid overclaiming. Mention tradeoffs briefly. Need answer in English. No need for citations. Need be careful not to include hidden thinking. Final should be just essay.\n\nNeed craft concise essay. Let's draft:\n\nTitle maybe. Paragraph 1: cloud convenient but not always right. Paragraph 2: privacy/data control: prompts/documents may be sensitive; local keeps data on device, reduces third-party access, compliance. Paragraph 3: cost and predictability: pay-per-token can grow; local fixed hardware cost, unlimited use, no rate limits. Paragraph 4: latency/offline/reliability: local works without internet, lower latency, consistent. Paragraph 5: control/customization: fine-tune, tune prompts, inspect weights, run open models, experiment. Paragraph 6: caveats: hardware limits, maintenance, cloud still better for scale/accessibility; local is choice for privacy/control/cost. Conclusion.\n\nNeed ensure \"short essay\". Maybe 350 words. Good.\n\nNeed final only."}}],"created":1795504301,"model":"/models/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF/Inkling-2-Mini-UD-Q3_K_XL.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b12651-d426a3774","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":512,"prompt_tokens":37,"total_tokens":549,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-TKmgfEBTQzsUSoGdyX9uZuAeiuI0Oy5d","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":37,"prompt_ms":185.109,"prompt_per_token_ms":5.002945945945946,"prompt_per_second":199.88223155005969,"predicted_n":512,"predicted_ms":9746.401,"predicted_per_token_ms":19.07319178082192,"predicted_per_second":52.429609657965024,"draft_n":530,"draft_n_accepted":245}}
